Camera group lifecycle and effective access
===========================================

Soft-deleted camera groups no longer contribute grants to CameraAccessService.
The group membership query checks organization and deleted_at before resolving
and merging the user's group grants. Historical memberships and grants may
remain stored; deleting them is not required for revocation to take effect.

Direct camera grants retain precedence. Active groups continue to merge their
permissions. Independent administrator or organization-role permissions remain
available. Deleting a restrictive group may therefore restore the user's role
permissions; group deletion is not a global deny or a user-account revocation.
The existing live-camera and organization check runs before all grants/roles.

Regression tests execute ORM queries against a minimal SQLite schema and verify
all five permission flags, deletion after an initial successful check, active
group merging, role fallback, direct grants and invalid-target controls. This
suite does not claim PostgreSQL schema/migration or HTTP authentication coverage;
those are separate release qualification checks. No hardware is accessed.

Current authority is checked at query time. This change does not fence a delete
that commits after the check, recall already delivered media, coordinate HLS
workers, or implement per-viewer stream leases.
